      "wikisort": 8,
      "xgboost": 1
    },
    "selection": "m_w = smallest power of two in {1,2,4,8,16} whose projected interval is >= 1.0 s, capped so that fuel stays <= 0.9 * 2^35; projection = instruction count of the candidate image / fastest instructions-per-second seen for that workload in the two previous rounds (30e9 when none); fixed before transfer, from local data only",
    "preregistrationSha256": "d0efbc4a76e1b2259516afc258cf3de09c33e2398aca7b6d4f3bf15c70f8bb45",
    "supersededPreregistrationSha256": "91e3daad713b8aa21827bc595454fc159f6cb18dcb549da0a9c879113eaa5449",
    "expectedValues": "benchmark fuel, verify fuel, result and the 17 arena counters at each n_w were re-derived from trusted reference images (round-51 originals; round-114 images agree), never from the measured compiler; exactly affine in m_w from >= 3 points except tarfind fuel, measured directly at n_w",
    "capChanges": [
      "qrduino KEXE_PAIRS 65536 -> 131072"
    ],
    "fullText": "/benchmarks/embench-official-20261015/protocol-revision.txt"
  },
  "exactness": "all 19 Kotoba samples matched the trusted-reference result, benchmark and verify fuel and all 17 arena counters at their n_w; all 19 C samples exact; the compiler passed 39 image compiles, 483 result/fuel/state observations and a 66,096-case differential test before measurement",
  "verifier": {
    "status": "PASS_INDEPENDENT_M93_RAW_CUSTODY_MULTIPLIER_FORMULA_V1",
    "output": "/benchmarks/embench-official-20261015/offline-verifier.txt"
  },
  "disclosures": [
    "Most of the gain comes from certified kernels: when a function's intermediate code exactly matches a recognized shape, the compiler emits hand-written AArch64 for it, with fuel accounting identical to the general path and a fallback to that path. Admission is by code shape, never by workload name, but the shapes were written for hot functions of these ports, so those speedups do not carry over to other programs automatically.",
    "nettle-sha256 uses the ARMv8 SHA-256 instructions; the C build (-O2, no intrinsics) does not. With a scalar sha256 path at its local estimate of about 1.27x, the geometric mean would be about 0.848.",
    "One measurement cycle on one host, one accepted sample per workload; no confidence interval is claimed.",
    "The projection used to choose m_w is not a lower bound (actual / projected interval ranged 0.67 to 1.76); every interval still cleared the 0.5 s floor (minimum 0.777 s, matmult-int).",
    "The Kotoba programs are translated ports. Using the upstream driver and formula does not make this a certified, unmodified Embench submission."
  ],
